# sdist membership (#689).
#
# Why this file exists at all, given #678 argued against it: setuptools has no
# pyproject.toml equivalent. Nothing under [tool.setuptools] reaches
# sdist.add_defaults, so MANIFEST.in is the only mechanism for changing sdist
# membership. The trade was made deliberately -- see CLAUDE.md.
#
# What it fixes: the distutils default membership glob is `tests/test*.py`,
# which matched all 141 test modules but not `tests/conftest.py`. The published
# 1.9.0 sdist therefore shipped a test suite that cannot be collected. Shipping
# the suite in runnable form is not reachable: 23 of those modules read `docs/`,
# `scripts/`, `examples/`, `uv.lock`, `CLAUDE.md`, and `.github/workflows/`, and
# the last would be rejected by check_sdist_contents.py's dotfile rule. So the
# suite comes out instead of the missing pieces going in. The tests remain in
# the repository and in CI; only the published sdist stops carrying them.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated because it is easy to lose: with this file present,
# popoto now has precondition 1 of the setuptools MANIFEST.in exclusion-bypass
# advisory (Unicode NFC/NFD collision on APFS/HFS+). The non-ASCII member rule
# in scripts/check_sdist_contents.py is therefore load-bearing, not
# defense-in-depth. Do not relax it to a warning.
prune tests
